        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "8.3(d)(7) The Company and the Union agree that, any provision in the parties' Collective Bargaining Agreements to the contrary notwithstanding, an employee may request that he or she be voluntarily laid off. If the request is approved by management, the employee will be coded as a layoff and will be regarded for all Company purposes as a laid off employee, except for purposes of layoff benefits under Article 21. The Union will be advised of all employees approved for voluntary layoff.",
